{"text":"Sunlight reaches Earth's atmosphere and scatters in all directions, but shorter blue wavelengths are scattered more strongly than longer red wavelengths due to a phenomenon known as Rayleigh scattering. This scattered blue light is redirected toward our eyes from all parts of the sky, creating the uniform blue appearance we observe during the day. Consequently, the sky looks blue rather than violet because our eyes are more sensitive to blue light and the solar spectrum emits less violet energy.","output_ids":[29108,4009,23716,8964,579,16078,321,1100,9872,303,660,17425,11,694,22602,6105,89661,513,35742,777,16025,1056,4860,2438,89661,4016,310,264,24057,3750,430,12870,60845,69377,13,1061,35742,6105,3000,369,47289,8574,1004,6213,494,660,5306,314,279,12515,11,6611,279,13398,6105,10771,567,22270,2261,279,1834,13,50275,11,279,12515,5686,6105,4598,1056,76990,1521,1004,6213,513,777,15739,310,6105,3000,321,279,12570,19142,70307,2599,76990,4649,13,248046],"meta_info":{"id":"c842ba716a524f139113de49a5b7bc63","finish_reason":{"type":"stop","matched":248046},"prompt_tokens":23,"weight_version":"default","num_retractions":0,"input_token_logprobs":[],"output_token_logprobs":[[-0.1832960546016693,29108,null],[-4.017272294731811e-05,4009,null],[-0.9026355147361755,23716,null],[-0.007720157038420439,8964,null],[-0.28569987416267395,579,null],[-0.0004538459761533886,16078,null],[-0.5541914701461792,321,null],[-0.38387808203697205,1100,null],[-0.0003212174342479557,9872,null],[-0.073560930788517,303,null],[-0.1265486180782318,660,null],[-0.0007445423980243504,17425,null],[-0.4449108839035034,11,null],[-0.9481990337371826,694,null],[-0.5586466789245605,22602,null],[-0.316119521856308,6105,null],[-0.058834150433540344,89661,null],[-0.3579278886318207,513,null],[-0.051745884120464325,35742,null],[-0.47542664408683777,777,null],[-0.141883984208107,16025,null],[-0.42673197388648987,1056,null],[-0.43808844685554504,4860,null],[-0.006252489984035492,2438,null],[-0.1076262816786766,89